  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Somalia Flood JR - World Vision</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Federal Government of Somalia has declared an emergency in areas where torrential deyr (October to December) rains, caused by El Ni&#xf1;o, have triggered floods. The number of people impacted by the seasonal rains and floods across Somalia has increased to over 2.4 million, according to the Somalia Disaster Management Agency (SoDMA), with over one million displaced and 110 killed in at least 36 districts. The UN has called it &quot;once-in-a-century&quot; floods, indicating the magnitude of the disaster. The rainshave resulted in significant flash floods, destruction or damage of shelters, roads, buildings, and bridges, and temporary displacement, mainly of internally displaced people in settlements.
The Dutch Relief Alliance is responding to the floods through the Somalia Flood Acute JointResponse, a consortium project with Oxfam Novib as lead. The partners will together implement a comprehensive emergency response inthe most affected areas including Baidoa, Bardhera, Beletweyne, Jowhar and Kismayo. Interventions include activities in the sectorsof Water, Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH), Health, Shelter/ Non-Food Items, Food Security and Multi-purpose Cash.</narrative>
  </description>
